This file marks this directory as the PUBLIC STUB of `sealwire-private`.

The real crate is proprietary and lives in a separate private repository.
`scripts/with-private.sh` swaps it over this directory for the duration of one
command, which deletes this file; the trap that restores the stub puts it back.

So: this file present = stub, absent = the private sources are in the tree.

Four things test exactly that, rather than looking for a module name that only
today's private crate happens to have:

  scripts/check-no-private.sh   refuses to commit while the private crate is in
  scripts/dev-full.mjs          picks --features private when it can
  scripts/restart-dev-cloud.sh  same, for the cloud dev loop
  scripts/task-team-e2e.mjs     skips itself instead of failing without them

Do not delete it, and do not add it to the private repository.
